# Member Portal Shell & Navigation Architecture

**Status:** **PENDING SIGN-OFF** — RFC promotion from Blueprint v9. **Not implementation authorization.**

**Source of truth:** [`docs/temp/DENALI-PORTAL-SHELL-NAVIGATION-BLUEPRINT.md`](../temp/DENALI-PORTAL-SHELL-NAVIGATION-BLUEPRINT.md) v9. This RFC distills that blueprint; it does not invent new architecture.

---

## 1. Overview

### 1.1 Problem (pre-PS-1) · current state (PS-2 landed 2026-07-05)

**Before PS-1:** Portal was a **registration-centric MVP** (P6-3) with inline nav in `app/me/layout.tsx`, hardcoded links, no platform shell frame.

**After PS-1:** Platform shell frame in `apps/portal/src/shell/*` — header, bottom nav, user menu (Profile + Logout). Inline layout nav removed.

**After PS-5 (2026-07-05):** Platform `home`, entitlements API + BFF proxy, shell nav gating, home aggregate, module dispatcher. **Next (PS-6):** plan-based entitlement deny rules, BFF cache, embedded hosts.

**Proof:** [IMPLEMENTATION-TRUTH-P6.md](./p6/appendices/IMPLEMENTATION-TRUTH-P6.md) PS-1/PS-2/PS-3 blocks · [builder-migration-contract.mdoc](./member-portal-shell/builder-migration-contract.mdoc) · GSH `GSH-PS3-*` tests · SMK-PTL-02..08.

### 1.2 Solution

Evolve to a **mobile-first Member Application Platform** via three platform extensions (unchanged from Blueprint):

1. **Member Module Registry** — workspace manifest block mirroring operator settings registry pattern
2. **Platform Portal Shell** — header, bottom nav (max 5 primary), hub, user menu, shell modes
3. **Member Entitlements BFF** — `GET /api/me/entitlements` intersected with registry for nav + route access

### 1.3 Routing audit verdict (2026-07-05)

Enterprise routing audit **confirmed** the design path — **no pivot**:

| KEEP | REFINE (documentation + implementation gates) |
| ---- | --------------------------------------------- |
| WRS host/surface model | WRS addendum ([wrs-portal-member-routing-addendum.mdoc](../standards/wrs-portal-member-routing-addendum.mdoc)) |
| `/me/*` member namespace | Bare `/me` redirect (DL-40) |
| `/catalog/*/register` outside shell | — |
| GSH cross-host builders | `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl` (DL-22) |
| Registry + Shell + Entitlements | URL freeze table §6 |

---

## 2. Goals

| ID | Goal |
| -- | ---- |
| G-01 | Manifest-driven member navigation — zero hardcoded nav in portal shell |
| G-02 | Workspace isolation — Urban can ship 2 modules with zero portal source edits |
| G-03 | Mobile-first shell — bottom nav, safe area, Telegram-ready (Phase 6 adapter) |
| G-04 | Scale to 50+ modules via registry + dispatcher without IA collapse |
| G-05 | API-enforced entitlements — decorative nav forbidden (DL-09) |
| G-06 | Preserve frozen URLs — `/me/registrations` alias permanent (DL-03, §6) |
| G-07 | PCMS + WRS compliance — marketing anonymous; no portal `/tours` |
| G-08 | Traceable guards + smoke — every invariant maps to guard or SMK-ID |

---

## 3. Non-goals

| ID | Non-goal |
| -- | -------- |
| NG-01 | Merge marketing and portal apps |
| NG-02 | Move registration under `/me/*` or member registry |
| NG-03 | Marketing authenticated session UI (PCMS) |
| NG-04 | Replace Tenant Kernel, WRS surfaces, PCMS, BFF pattern, profile INV-MP-* |
| NG-05 | Operator finance routes on portal BFF (DL-15) |
| NG-06 | `pluginId ===` branching in `apps/portal` (INV-MP-05) |
| NG-07 | Per-module portal `layout.tsx` forks |
| NG-08 | Client-only entitlement gating |
| NG-09 | Portal SEO / public catalog browsing |

---

## 4. Architecture

### 4.1 Frozen contracts (unchanged)

| Contract | Authority |
| -------- | --------- |
| Tenant Kernel / host parsing | `packages/tenant-kernel` |
| WRS-001 surfaces | [workspace-routing-standard.mdoc](../standards/workspace-routing-standard.mdoc) |
| PCMS-001 member session | [member-session-portal-authority.mdoc](../standards/member-session-portal-authority.mdoc) |
| Profile capability model | [platform-portal-member-profile.mdoc](./platform-portal-member-profile.mdoc) |
| Registration intake | [platform-portal-registration-intake.mdoc](./platform-portal-registration-intake.mdoc) |
| BFF + `buildMemberApiHeaders` | [platform-portal-member.mdoc](./platform-portal-member.mdoc) |
| Guest Surface Host URL builders | `packages/guest-surface-host` |
| Theme cascade | P6 theming docs |

### 4.2 Platform vs workspace ownership

| Platform owns | Workspace owns |
| ------------- | -------------- |
| Shell frame, slots, nav tier caps | `memberPortal` manifest block |
| Shell modes (minimal / full / redirect) | Module API + BFF upstream logic |
| Session/tenant presentation | Entitlement rule declarations |
| Cross-surface egress rendering (GSH) | Registration flow steps |
| Codegen validation (mirror settings registry) | `memberProfile` field capabilities |
| Entitlements BFF surface | Portal theme skin content |

### 4.3 Member Module Registry

Mirrors operator `SettingsModuleManifest` pattern:

| Operator (shipped) | Member (RFC) |
| ------------------ | ------------ |
| `SettingsModuleManifest` | Member module manifest types |
| `operatorSettings` in workspace manifest | `memberPortal` block |
| `operator.settings.{moduleId}` CASL | `member.module.{moduleId}` entitlement |
| Settings hub in `apps/web` | Portal module hub + bottom nav |
| Codegen → generated resolver | Codegen → `resolveMemberPortalModules(pluginId)` |

**Conflict rules (codegen fail-closed):** duplicate ids, >5 primary tier, reserved ids (DL-30), invalid route roots, workspace declaration of platform-owned ids.

#### 4.3.1 Platform-owned vs workspace-owned modules (DL-30)

| Class | Module ids | Route | Workspace manifest | Owner |
| ----- | ---------- | ----- | ------------------ | ----- |
| **Platform-owned** | `home` | `/me/home` | **MUST NOT declare** | Platform shell — shipped BP-4 |
| **Workspace-owned** | `trips`, `profile`, `wallet`, … | manifest `routePath` | Declared in `memberPortal` | Workspace |
| **Namespace-reserved** | `more`, `api`, `catalog` | n/a | **MUST NOT declare** | Shell / routing namespace |

**Why `home` does not conflict with `/me/home`:** The **route** `/me/home` is a platform-delivered page. The **module id** `home` is reserved so workspaces cannot collide with the platform home module or override its route. Workspaces reference `home` in nav tiers by id, but the module definition lives in **platform registry defaults**, not workspace manifest.

**Registry validation:** Codegen rejects `memberPortal.modules[].id === "home"` with `RESERVED-PLATFORM-OWNED`. Platform injects `home` into effective registry at runtime/codegen merge.

**Migration:** Phase 2 codegen active; platform `home` stub in generated registry Phase 4; no workspace manifest entry ever required.

### 4.4 Member Entitlements (DL-09)

**Wire format:** `GET /api/me/entitlements` portal BFF → API member entitlements upstream.

**Not chosen:** JWT embed (PCMS scope); client-only fetch (wrong first paint).

**Shell rule:** `navModules = registryModules ∩ entitlements.granted`.

See [platform-portal-member-entitlements.mdoc](./platform-portal-member-entitlements.mdoc). Exact upstream API schema: Phase 5 implementation PR.

### 4.5 Shell state machine

| State | Entry | Chrome |
| ----- | ----- | ------ |
| `REDIRECT_UNAUTH` | No JWT on `/me/*` | None → `/` |
| `REDIRECT_AUTH_HOME` | Valid JWT on `/` | None → default module |
| `REGISTRATION_MINIMAL` | `/catalog/*/register` | Brand + back egress only |
| `MEMBER_FULL` | Valid JWT on `/me/*` | Header + bottom nav + outlet |
| `API_MEMBER` | `/api/me/*` | No shell |

**Invariant:** Never `MEMBER_FULL` on registration path (DL-01).

### 4.6 Guest conformance L4 (DL-07)

**L4** = L3 guest conformance + `guestConformance.memberApp: true` + `memberPortal.availability` ≠ `off` (see [member-portal-registry-schema.mdoc](./member-portal-shell/member-portal-registry-schema.mdoc) §6).

Enforced by `guard-member-portal-contract.mjs` (DL-18 superseded 2026-07-06).

